A macro call resolved from a stubbed config lands its pinned value in the file through the
same typed write as a literal — the stub short-circuits, so nothing executes.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
status: backlog
---
# My Plan

- [ ] 3 SP: Task one
- [ ] 2 SP: Task two
-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
macro_stubs:
  core.macros.date: 19700101-00-00
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md created="{{ macro('core.macros.date') }}"
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 ---
 title: Foo
 status: backlog
+created: 19700101-00-00
 ---
 # My Plan
 
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: created=19700101-00-00
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
status: backlog
created: 19700101-00-00
---
# My Plan

- [ ] 3 SP: Task one
- [ ] 2 SP: Task two
